                    insight_sustainable:    `Sustainable leadership: all four KPIs on a credible recovery — engagement back above 60, wellbeing rebuilt, the bottleneck cleared and Atlas defensible. You treated isolation as the root cause and built support architecture that outlives the crisis.`,
                    insight_pyrrhic:        `A Pyrrhic delivery: Atlas looks on track but you spent the people and the leader to get there. Burnout and attrition re-risk the very delivery you protected — the date you "made" is built on collapsing foundations.`,
                    insight_thin:           `You hit delivery but the leadership is thin. Without rebuilt wellbeing and engagement the result is fragile, and the next pressure finds the same isolated leader and the same bottleneck.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of a credible recovery across the four KPIs. The most likely cause: you treated the symptoms — effort, schedule, the team — instead of the isolation and non-delegation underneath them.`,
                    insight_lowwellbeing:   `Leader-wellbeing stayed low. Chronic overload degrades exactly the judgment a high-stakes deadline demands — wellbeing and performance are coupled, not opposed.`,
                    insight_nosupport:      `You never stood up a real support relationship. The coach or peer board is most needed when time is scarcest — without it, Elena kept deciding alone and decision quality suffered.`,
                    insight_rivallost:      `You lost the internal rival — and with him the legacy-integration knowledge and weeks of Atlas time. Relationship repair was a delivery lever, not a soft extra.`,
                    insight_rivalkept:      `You repaired the rival relationship. Trusting the passed-over lead with a real mandate kept the institutional knowledge and turned a threat into a contributor.`,
                    insight_greentheatre:   `You projected false confidence to the board at least once. Green theatre spends credibility you can't get back — and a new leader needs that credibility most when the project is amber.`,
                    insight_architecture:   `You built genuine support architecture — confidential support, delegation with escalation thresholds, and a sustainable rhythm. That is the infrastructure that lets a senior leader perform without burning out.`,

